   "text": "I read this as a lipidated cyclic peptide, a Pen\u2013Pen disulfide macrocycle with two \u03b3Glu\u2013(AEEA)\u2082\u2013acyl side chains. Two features of the SMILES are guesses rather than clear readings of the drawing: the acyl chain lengths and the naphthalene attachment position.\n\n**Backbone, N-terminus to C-terminus**\n- Pen1 is acylated on its amine with the first lipid arm: palmitoyl\u2013\u03b3Glu\u2013AEEA\u2013AEEA. The AEEA unit is \u2013NH\u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082\u2013O\u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082\u2013O\u2013CH\u2082\u2013C(=O)\u2013. Pen1 sits at the top of the ring.\n- The ring continues through Asn, Thr, 7-methyl-Trp and Lys to Pen2, which closes the ring through the S\u2013S bond to Pen1.\n- Lys carries the second lipid arm on its side-chain amine: AEEA\u2013AEEA\u2013\u03b3Glu\u2013palmitoyl.\n- After Pen2 the chain runs Tyr(O-CH\u2082CH\u2082NH\u2082), 2-naphthylalanine, 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid, Glu, Asn and 3-pyridylalanine.\n- The C-terminus is N-methylglycinamide, \u2013N(CH\u2083)CH\u2082C(=O)NH\u2082.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI worked each wedge or hash out by CIP priorities. Every amino acid centre comes out as the natural L form: Pen R, Asn S, Thr S, Trp S, Lys S, Tyr S, 2-Nal S, Glu S, Pya S, and both lipid-arm Glu S. The Thr \u03b2-carbon has no clear wedge, so I assumed the natural L-Thr (3R) configuration.\n\n**Uncertain points**\n- The acyl chains are cut off or hard to count in the image. I took both as palmitoyl (C16), but the pixel lengths fit 14\u201315 bonds about as well.\n- I took the naphthalene as 2-naphthyl.\n\nSMILES: CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)